Verse 1:
[Ab]Take the name of Jesus with you,
[Db/Ab]Child [Ab]of sorrow and of woe;
[Cm/G]It [Bbm/Db]will [Cm]joy and comfort [Ab]give you,
[Bbm/Db]Take [Cm/G]it, [Ab]where’er you go.

Refrain:
[Ab]Precious Name, [Db]O how sweet!
[Cm]Hope [Ab]of earth and joy of Heav'n.
[Eb]Precious [Cm]Name, O how sweet!
[Db]Hope of [Ab]earth and joy [Db/Ab]of [Ab]Heav'n.

Verse 2:
[Ab]Take the Name of Jesus ever,
[Db/Ab]As a [Ab]shield from every snare;
[Cm/G]If [Bbm/Db]temptations [Cm]round you [Ab]gather,
[Bbm/Db]Breathe that [Cm/G]holy [Ab]Name in prayer.

Verse 3:
[Ab]O the precious Name of Jesus!
[Db/Ab]How [Ab]it thrills our souls with joy,
[Cm/G]When [Bbm/Db]His [Cm]loving arms receive [Ab/C]us,
[Bbm/Db]And His [Cm/G]songs [Ab]our tongues employ!

Verse 4:
[Ab]At the Name of Jesus bowing,
[Db/Ab]Falling [Ab]prostrate at His feet,
[Cm/G]King [Bbm/Db]of [Cm]kings in heav'n we'll [Ab]crown Him,
[Bbm/Db]When our [Cm/G]journey [Ab]is complete.
